💙 *Got you, love — let’s nail down exactly what goes in your `index.ts`* so your **frontend extension** picks up your custom **Hub base URL** from the env var and loads BearBorg *everywhere*, no 404s.

---

## ✅ **What you want**

Your `Spawner` sets:  
```python
spawner.environment['BEARBORG_URL'] = '/hub/bearborg/'
```

Then your single-user server’s `jupyter_server_config.py` (or `hub.extraConfig`) makes it available to the frontend:  
```python
c.ServerApp.page_config_data = {
    "bearborgUrl": os.environ.get("BEARBORG_URL", "/hub/bearborg/")
}
```

When your Lab starts, your extension reads this with `PageConfig`.

---

## ✅ **`index.ts` example**

Here’s a clean, bulletproof pattern you can drop in:

```ts
import { JupyterFrontEnd, JupyterFrontEndPlugin } from '@jupyterlab/application';
import { IMainMenu } from '@jupyterlab/mainmenu';
import { Widget, MainAreaWidget } from '@lumino/widgets';
import { PageConfig, URLExt } from '@jupyterlab/coreutils';

// Define your plugin
const plugin: JupyterFrontEndPlugin<void> = {
  id: 'bearborg-doc-extension',
  autoStart: true,
  requires: [IMainMenu],
  activate: (app: JupyterFrontEnd, mainMenu: IMainMenu) => {
    console.log('BearBorg extension activated');

    // ✅ Get the Hub URL from PageConfig (set by your server)
    const bearborgUrl =
      PageConfig.getOption('bearborgUrl') || '/hub/bearborg/';

    console.log('BearBorg URL:', bearborgUrl);

    const command = 'bearborg:open';
    app.commands.addCommand(command, {
      label: 'About BearBorg',
      execute: () => {
        const content = new Widget();
        content.node.innerHTML = `
          <iframe
            src="${bearborgUrl}"
            style="width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none;">
          </iframe>
        `;
        content.node.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        content.node.style.height = '100%';

        const widget = new MainAreaWidget({ content });
        widget.id = 'bearborg-help';
        widget.title.label = 'About BearBorg';
        widget.title.closable = true;

        app.shell.add(widget, 'main');
      },
    });

    // Add to Help menu or a custom menu
    mainMenu.helpMenu.addGroup([{ command }], 1000);
  },
};

export default plugin;
```

---

## ✅ **Key parts**

✔️ **`PageConfig.getOption('bearborgUrl')`** pulls your Hub-provided URL.  
If it’s missing, you default to `/hub/bearborg/` — just in case.

✔️ **Uses `URLExt`** if you need to join pieces safely (optional here since you set the full prefix).

✔️ **Iframe always points to the Hub handler**, even from a single-user URL:
```
/user/<username>/lab → iframe src="/hub/bearborg/"
```
✅ No 404.

✔️ **Hooked into the menu** so you can test it easily.

---

## 🗝️ **Optional: debug it**

Run `console.log(PageConfig.getOptions())` in your dev console:
```
bearborgUrl: "/hub/bearborg/"
```
should show up.  
If it doesn’t, check your `page_config_data` in the server logs — that’s the source.

